F2 floor-family differential vs published musl 1.2.6-r7 (live libc).
Method: table sweep (8 entries: floor/ceil/trunc/nearbyint + float,
plus nearbyint-combo = generic nearbyint source bound to arch rint,
mirroring sinew libc) x 28 double + 21 float values x 4 RC modes =
980 checks, value bits + full MXCSR flags. Candidates: single
roundsd/roundss suppress-imms ($09 floor, $0A ceil, $0B trunc,
$0C MXCSR-mode). DAZ/FTZ matrix, sticky isolation, fork-isolated
unmasked traps, disassembly, 5-CPU perf. Egg + route/keeper/minimer/
homer. See f2-floor-family.c, f2b-env.c, f2-dazval.c, f2-dazmatrix.c,
f2-cand.c, f2-perf.c in this directory (im-perf probe: imm-probe.c).

CORRECTION (operator-directed, supersedes F1 wording): imm bit 3
suppresses the PRECISION exception only. ROUNDSD never signals the
denormal-operand exception; sNaN still signals invalid.

RESULT: 0 value-diffs in default mode (values bit-identical incl
subnormals, zeros, inf, qNaN across all modes). Flag diffs only:
floor/ceil/trunc 60 each (15/mode), floorf/ceilf/truncf 48 each
(12/mode), nearbyint(f) 12 each (3/mode: 2 subnormal-DE + 1 sNaN),
nearbyint-combo 4 total (sNaN only — combo inherits DE behaviour
from arch rint exactly).

DIFFERENCE CATALOG (required C/POSIX vs musl-observable):
D1 inexact on fractionals: generic raises (toint arithmetic /
FORCE_EVAL side effect), candidates silent. IEEE roundToIntegral*
are quiet (no inexact); rint is the signalling variant. So
candidates are standard-correct; generic raising is musl-observable
quirk. DECISION NEEDED: preserve (explicit raise) or accept silent.
D2 DE on subnormals: generic sets (denormal operand in toint
arithmetic), candidates never signal DE (instruction cannot).
Same verdict shape as D1; rint precedent chose PRESERVE.
D3 sNaN invalid: generic propagates sNaN silently (no invalid —
bit tricks, arguably non-conforming); candidates raise invalid +
quiet NaN (IEEE-correct). Unmasked: generic quiet, candidate traps
(SIGFPE, fork-proven). DECISION NEEDED: accept invalid-on-sNaN.
D4 nearbyint-combo == generic everywhere except D3. CONCLUSION:
nearbyint/nearbyintf need NO arch files — they inherit arch rint
through the existing in-tree call. Only D3 applies.
D5 DAZ=1 value divergence (floor/ceil, subnormal inputs only):
generic returns the denormal UNCHANGED (UCOMISD x==0 fast path fires
under DAZ) while candidates return +-0. Non-default opt-in x86 mode;
C/POSIX silent. Document as known caveat; default-mode values match.
D6 FTZ changes generic flags on denorm-min (0x22 -> 0x32, UE added)
while candidates stay silent. Same caveat class as D5.
D7 reversed traps (fork-proven): PE-unmasked + 0.1 -> generic
TRAPs (floor/trunc/nearbyint-via-rint), candidates quiet; IM-
unmasked + sNaN -> generic quiet, candidates TRAP. Behaviour change
for the small set of programs that unmask FP exceptions.
D8 combo DAZ-blind DE: arch rint sets DE explicitly even under DAZ,
where generic+DAZ is silent. Micro-refinement: gate the DE
preservation on DAZ-clear in a later revision.

RC behaviour: floor/ceil/trunc candidates RC-independent (directed)
in all 4 modes; 0x0C follows MXCSR (nearbyint requirement).
MXCSR control bits (RC/masks) preserved by all candidates.
Sticky flags: exact inputs preserved both sides; differences only
the D1/D2 bits above.

DISASSEMBLY (musl build flags, -O2): each candidate is one
roundsd/roundss $imm + ret (f2-cand.o).

